From 2f07c1bc2cc007b3f815e063fc839682c95513ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 17:45:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make Concrete baseline a faithful k-channel selector
 (ConcreteSelectorK)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the B-channel soft-mask ConcreteSelect with ConcreteSelectorK, a
faithful supervised concrete selector (cf. Balin et al. 2019, App. G):
k Concrete/Gumbel-softmax selector nodes each pick one band and output
z_j = sum_b w_jb * x_b — a k-channel convex combination that preserves
signal magnitude, eliminating the input-attenuation artifact of the old
B-channel mask. Temperature anneals exponentially T0=10.0 -> TB=0.01 as
in the original paper. The topk DiagonalBandGate path is unchanged.

- model/modules.py: ConcreteSelect -> ConcreteSelectorK (k-channel
  output, exponential anneal, same set_progress/selected_bands API,
  collision fill-up to exactly k distinct bands at inference).
- model/model.py: SegmentationModel takes encoder_in_channels;
  build_model sizes the encoder with in_channels=k for the concrete
  branch (B for topk/none).
- train.py: reload best_model.pth before writing selected_bands.json so
  the recorded selection matches the deployed model, not the last epoch;
  also store "selected_bands" inside the best checkpoint.
- configs/concrete_k3.yaml: T0=10.0/TB=0.01 (exponential), 500 epochs,
  patience 70.
- scripts/run_gate_batch.py: the --concrete arm overrides the base
  config's gate tau with T0=10.0/TB=0.01.
- README.md: update the baseline description to the k-channel semantics.

Verified without real data: concrete model from concrete_k3.yaml maps
(2,15,64,64) -> (2,2,64,64) with encoder in_channels=3, returns 3
distinct bands, T(0)=10 / T(0.5)=0.316 / T(1)=0.01, preserves constant
inputs exactly in train and eval, grads flow to alpha, state_dict
round-trips; topk gate_k3 path and no-gate baseline are unaffected.

